From 796397b1e762d3a5da7804adb4bdd1bd3e432fc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:33:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 155/156] webrender: shaders without bitwise ops, switch and
 array returns

For GLSL ES 1.00, written so that every version compiles the same code:
- bit fields through WR_BITS, WR_HAS_FLAG, WR_SHL, WR_SHR and WR_MOD
  (base.glsl), the operators themselves on GL and ES 3, float arithmetic
  on ESSL 1 (exact below 2^24); highp int in ESSL 1 fragment shaders
- every switch as an if/else chain (tools: switch2if.py)
- the multi-texel GPU buffer fetches through WR_GPU_BUFFER_FETCH_<n>,
  out-array functions on ESSL 1
- uint constants and the texel fetch address math without uint on ESSL 1
- texelFetch macros and wr_mix/wr_transpose/wr_inverse/wr_round for the
  ESSL 1 rewrite in webrender_build

The 1471 wrench reftests under GL 3 (Mesa llvmpipe) give exactly the
same results as with the original shaders (the same 93 tests differ by
the same pixels).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
